===Etymology===
{{ja-kanjitab|しゃく|yomi=kanyoon}}

Coined in Japan as a {{m|ja|国字|tr=kokuji||national (i.e. coined-in-Japan) character}},<ref name="KDJ2">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2}}</ref><ref name="DDJS">{{R:Digital-Daijisen}}</ref><ref name="K">{{R:Kojien}}</ref> from elements {{m|mul|疒|t=[[illness]]|pos=[[radical]]}} + {{m|mul|積|t=[[accumulation]]}}.  The original sense was {{m|en|[[menstrual]] [[cramps]]}}, and the character was coined from the way that this physical pain happens a lot over time.<ref name="KDJ2"/>

The reading comes from the [[呉音#Japanese|goon]] reading ''shaku'' of constituent part {{m|ja|積}}.<ref name="KDJ2"/>

First cited in 1593.<ref name="KDJ2"/>

