=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|possession particle}} {{lang|zh|的}} is usually omitted when referring to a close relationship (family, close friends) or to an institutional or organizational relationship (school, work).
*: {{zh-x|這 是 我 媽媽{ma}|This is my mother}}
*: {{zh-x|這 是 我們 學校|This is our school}}
* {{sense|particle linking a noun and an adjective}} {{lang|zh|的}} is omitted if it is used with a single-syllable adjective.
*: {{zh-x|壞人|bad person}}
* It must be used when the adjective has more than one syllable or if the adjective is qualified by an adverb.
*: {{zh-x|奇怪 的 人|strange person}}
*: {{zh-x|很 好 的 茶|a very good tea}}
* {{lang|zh|的}} is also omitted when the association is frequent
*: {{zh-x|中國人|Chinese people}}
* When necessary, the character {{lang|zh|的}} is referred to as {{zh-l|白勺的|tr=bái sháo de}} to differentiate it from the homophones {{zh-l|得*}} ({{zh-l|雙人得|tr=shuāng rén dé}}) and {{zh-l|地*}} ({{zh-l|土也地|tr=tǔ yě dì}}). In addition, these three particles should not to be confused with each other. Compare these three phrases:
*: {{zh-x|無奈 的 嘆息|helpless sigh}}
*: {{zh-x|無奈 地{de} 嘆息|sigh helplessly}}
*: {{zh-x|無奈 得{de} 嘆息|feel helpless with sighing}}
* In Mandarin slang usage, {{lang|zh|的}} can be pronounced as ''di'', and substituted by the character {{zh-l|滴}} in writing:
*: {{zh-x|好 滴{di}|okay}}'' (where the standard form is "{{lang|zh|[[好的]]}}")''

